<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Feed group buys 54,000T US corn at tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Feed group buys 54,000T US corn at tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Members Feed Industry Group bought a 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. No.2 corn from Garnac at a tender on Tuesday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The feed group's main buyers are Taiwan's Formosa Oilseed, Fomau Cereal, Morn Sun Feed Mill and Shin Tai Indusry.</p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis, traders said.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Tonnage   Date/Location		     Price/Futures</p>
<p>	     U.S. Gulf   Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> 27,000    March 8-22  March 23-April 6  US$143.50</p>
<p> 27,000    March 8-22  March 23-April 6  94.80 US cents/May</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
